<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Shell to close Australian coal mine.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Shell to close Australian coal mine.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell Group unit Bellambi Colleries Pty Ltd said it will phase out coal production from the South Bulli Colliery in southern New South Wales between April and August 1997, costing 275 jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;Although a marginal operation for several years, geological difficulties have now increased operating costs to a level at which the mine is no longer economically viable,&quot; Bellambi said in a statement.</p>
<p>South Bulli, Australia's oldest coal mine, has produced nearly 70 million tonnes of coal since the 1880s, Bellambi said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
